out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('13.7  Review & Mediate: The job description and the person reading it'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 13 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _before I **sent** it._   **2** _…whether we have procedures, **then** yes._   **3** _…appointed in August **to a post which** did not exist in March._   **4** _He decided **to apply** for the post…_   **5** _He **drew** on four terms…_   **6** _A question **whose** answer you can predict…_'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **A record of an argument that happened in a room you were not in.** **_Or equivalent experience_ is there because somebody fought for it**, probably after losing a good candidate to the sentence before it — **and every strange clause in a job description is a scar.** **The one question:** _if I could do the work, would this line still matter?_ **If no, it is a proxy.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The finding of this cycle has a life well beyond the examination and it should be stated flatly: a requirement that cannot be failed is not a requirement, it is a reserve power.** **Nobody has ever been rejected on _excellent communication skills_.** The line is on the page **so that a panel can refuse somebody without writing down the real reason** — and Mr Barghouti, who drafts these, says he has watched it done twice and done it once. ⚠ **Do not soften that.** The class contains people who will write such pages, **and 16.1 is where they learn to write criteria that can be failed** — **so plant it here and name the cycle.**'));
out.push(A('**There are two ways to misread a job description and the confident reader\'s way is the one nobody warns about.** The first reader stops at _five years_ and does not apply. ⚠ **The second reads the Desirable list as a scoreboard**, adds up his eleven years and three systems and bids for the top of the band — **and Desirable lines do not add up to a stronger claim.** **They are what the panel will settle for if nobody has the Essential ones.** **He is bidding on the wrong column**, and in most classes he is the student who is certain he already knows this cycle. ⚠ **Make the room mark both readers wrong before anybody is told which one is the better candidate.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('No Practise line in x.7; the Language box in this cycle carries the three moves and the warning. ⚠ **The warning is the one to enforce: do not tell either reader what to do.** The mediator\'s work is **the three moves and the one question**, and advice given here is **advice about somebody else\'s career from somebody who has read one page of it.**'));
